: (Lawful or Chaotic) blessed +2 longsword named Frost Brand
: 	reason: by use of a helm of opposite alignment, it is possible for
: 		a Lawful character to get Chaotic weapons, a Chaotic 
: 		character to get Lawful weapons, and a Neutral character to
: 		get all artifacts.  It isn't possible for a L or C character
: 		to get Neutral weapons, though.

True, but WHY?  It's rather odd to wish for an inferior weapon, just for
the sake of generating a complete collection of artifacts.  I just wish
for Stormy or Mjollnir, and with Excaliber as an easily gained
rustproof backup, I'm good to go for the entire game!
: 
: armor:
: blessed +2 gray dragon scale mail
: 	reason: the best body armor to be had, dragon scale mail adds 9
: 		to your AC before the plus.  Gray dragon scale mail gives
: 		the wearer resistance to magic which, unlike all the other
: 		forms of dragon scale, cannot be gained by eating the 
: 		dragon's corpse.  It can be had by a cloak, but this allows
: 		the wearer to wear a different cloak and still have magic
: 		protection.

I usually go for +3, just a small preference.  Tougher odds, though.
Knowing I can probably make it anyway later on, I'll reserve this wish
for later on.
:
: blessed +2 boots of speed
: 	reason: simply the most useful boots to be had.

RIGHT!  Wish numero uno, hands down.
: 
: blessed +2 elven cloak
: 	reason: stealth is a much more important ability than protection
: 		or displacement.  Invisibility can be gained without the
: 		use of a cloak or rings (though I wouldn't advise this until
: 		you have an alternate method of entering shops), and magic
: 		resistance can be had via body armor (see above)

But the first barracks you find, and presto...a collection of these.
Still, if you're low level and desperate, not a bad investment :)
I prefer displacement in general.
: 
: 
: blessed +2 shield of reflection
: 	reason: It's the only shield that gives any extra abilities, plus
: 		it lowers your AC by 2 before the plus and is naturally
: 		rust-proof.
: 
Very, very good wish.  Can't be intrinsically gained, and stops all
those dragons from annihiliating you from off-screen (grrr...).

: amulets:
: blessed amulet of life saving
: 	reason: there's no better proof against stupid deaths.
: 
Never leave home without it!

: potions:
: 3 potions of gain level (blessed or uncursed makes little difference)
: 	reason: should be obvious
:
Blessed give you next level + 1/2 xp to the next after that.
Still not much difference when you're using 3 in a row, but worth
pointing out.  Smart way to use this is drink one every other level,
to maximize the benefits...unless you need huge xp amounts to
advance anyway.
: 
: scrolls:
: 3 blessed scrolls of enchant [weapon, armor]
: 
: 3 blessed scrolls of remove curse
: 	reason: I always seem to have something that needs un-cursing.
: 
: 3 blessed scrolls of genocide
: 
: 3 cursed scrolls of genocide
: 	reason: Good for summoning large numbers of Wraiths, Nurses, or
: 		some monster that will give me an intrinsic I don't yet have.
: 
All good, but I find a blessed magic marker can often gain you more in
the end (depends on the circumstances).

: gems & stones:
: a blessed luckstone
: 	reason: blessed luckstones only affect your luck if it is positive.
: 		uncursed luckstones maintain your luck at its current level
: 		regardless if it is good or bad.
: 
Yes!  Just don't let it get cursed...

: tools:
: a blessed blindfold (if I don't already have one)
: 
: a blessed magic marker
: 	reason: for making blessed scrolls.
: 
: a blessed tinning kit
: 	reason: for making blessed tins, in case I lose an intrinsic.
: 		(If I get hungry, I'll eat the corpse)
: 
: a blessed stethoscope
: 
Easy to polypile (if you're into that sort of thing...:)  If you have
no moral hang-ups about that, then wish for a blessed wand of polymorph
instead.

: rings:
: a blessed ring of conflict
: 
: a blessed ring of levitation
: 
: a blessed +5 ring of protection
